    "result_text": "The build is green: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, dropping the per-city sequence numbers entirely. Everything derived from the code follows automatically.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New `util/Regions.java`** \u2014 a single `forPostcode(String)` rule that maps a 4-digit postcode to its region (NSW/VIC/QLD) or `\"UNKNOWN\"`. This is the one place the `<REGION>` rule lives.\n\n2. **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 rewrote `generateCustomerCode` to produce `Regions.forPostcode(postcode) + \"-\" + hash8(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`, where `hash8` is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256. Removed the old per-city sequence counting and the now-unused `prefix3` helper. The telephone is already E.164-normalized by the mapper before save, so it is the normalized form.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `formatLocality` now reads the locality off the identity (the `<REGION>` segment of the `customerCode`), falling back to `Regions.forPostcode` only for owners with no code yet (e.g. seed data), which yields the same value. Removed the obsolete city/region lookup tables and the unused `Map` import, and refreshed the doc examples for the check digit and membership number.\n\nValues built from `customerCode` needed no logic changes and inherit the new identity automatically:\n- **Membership number** (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) \u2192 e.g. `NSW-3F5A9C2E-M26`\n- **Check digit** \u2014 Luhn over the digits in the new code\n- **Create audit record** in `OwnerRestControllerV1` \u2014 already logs `customerCode` (confirmed: `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E ...`)\n\nThe new code `NSW-16E6609E` fits the existing `customer_code VARCHAR(20)` column (max length `UNKNOWN-XXXXXXXX` = 16). The acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` passes.",
