    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a clean, idiomatic refactor:\n\n- **The `Regions` extraction is the right move.** The postcode\u2192region derivation previously lived inline in `OwnerMapper.formatLocality`, but the new identity needs the same rule in `ClinicServiceImpl.generateCustomerCode`. Pulling it into `util.Regions` (private constructor, static `forPostcode`, focused Javadoc) gives both call sites a single source of truth and matches the existing `util` package neighbours (`AddressNormalizer`, `E164Telephone`). No duplicated range table.\n\n- **`hash8` is scoped correctly.** It's used only by `generateCustomerCode`, so leaving it as a private static helper in the service \u2014 rather than over-extracting it to a util \u2014 is the natural choice and parallels the old `prefix3` helper it replaces. Regions was extracted because it's shared; hash8 wasn't because it isn't.\n\n- **Downstream derivations stay where they belong.** `formatLocality`, `formatCheckDigit`, and `formatMembershipNumber` all continue to read from `customerCode`, so the identity change propagates through them without new coupling; `formatLocality` reading the region as the pre-hyphen segment (with a postcode fallback) is simple and self-contained.\n\n- **No class is becoming a catch-all**, and the dead `java.util.Map` import was removed from the mapper. Javadoc was updated consistently (including the worked examples) in the same house style.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find the result natural.",
